{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UserInterfaceSizeClass","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You receive a size class value when you read either the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"EnvironmentValues\/horizontalSizeClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"EnvironmentValues\/verticalSizeClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value. The value tells"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you about the amount of space available to your views in a given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"direction. You can read the size class like any other of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", by creating a property with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property wrapper:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["@Environment(\\.horizontalSizeClass) private var horizontalSizeClass","@Environment(\\.verticalSizeClass) private var verticalSizeClass"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSwiftUI sets the size class based on several factors, including:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The current device type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The orientation of the device.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type"